# Canonical identity for this repository's history.
#
# Early commits were made under two other identities, one of which
# (<landon>) is not a valid email address. Those commits are already
# published, so rewriting them is not an option — this maps them to the
# canonical identity for `git log`, `git shortlog -sne`, and `git blame`.
#
# Note: GitHub's web UI does not read .mailmap. To have GitHub attribute the
# <landonmiles@me.com> commits, add that address to your GitHub account.

jlm <josephlandonmiles@gmail.com> JLM <landonmiles@me.com>
jlm <josephlandonmiles@gmail.com> jlm <landon>
